# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers static assets (see DEPLOYMENT.md).
# Not served itself. Every rule that matches a path adds its headers, and a
# header set by two rules gets both values joined with a comma, so the
# /_astro/* rule detaches ("! ") the Cache-Control from /* before setting its
# own. scripts/check-build.mjs fails the build if a line here goes missing or
# any built file would get two Cache-Control values.

# Every response: pages, the 404 page, icons, robots.txt, sitemap.xml.
# no-cache: always revalidated (ETag), because the data changes every night.
# no-transform: Cloudflare must not change the pages (e.g. inject its
# analytics beacon). The CSP header only adds frame-ancestors; the full policy
# stays in each page's <meta> tag.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-transform

# Astro's hashed files (CSS, JavaScript, fonts): a new name for every change,
# so they never need revalidating.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
